Short:        Fast Quake for 68060 + RTG, 8/16 bpp, AHI sound
Author:       andrzej79
Type:         game/shoot
Version:      0.9b
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1
Requires:     68060 with FPU, Picasso96, AHI v4 (for sound)

WarpQuake 0.9b
==============

Quake for AmigaOS 3.x on a 68060 with an RTG (Picasso96) screen. It was
written for CS-Lab's Warp accelerators and is fast on any 68060.

It is id Software's own software renderer, kept bit-exact with id's C code,
with its hot paths rewritten in 68060 assembly. timedemo demo1 at 320x200 on
a 68060 at 108 MHz runs at 26.3 fps at 8 bpp and 23.7 fps at 16 bpp (without
sound).

Features
--------

- 8-bit CLUT or 16-bit RGB screens, any mode from 320x200 to 1280x1024,
  switchable in the game (Options / Video Options). At 16 bpp the lighting
  is computed per colour instead of rounded to the 256-colour palette, and
  water tints blue.
- Sound through AHI, any audio mode, 11025 to 44100 Hz (Options / Sound
  Options).
- Raw mouse input: neither accelerated nor dropped.

Requirements
------------

- A 68060 with its FPU (and 68060.library).
- AmigaOS 3.1 or later.
- Picasso96 (RTG) with 8-bit and/or 16-bit screen modes.
- About 32 MB of free fast RAM (16 MB for the game, plus the screen and the
  surface cache).
- AHI v4 for sound (optional).
- Quake's game data, which is not included: pak0.pak from the shareware or
  registered version, and pak1.pak from the registered version.

Installation
------------

Copy the WarpQuake drawer anywhere, then copy your Quake data into an id1
drawer inside it:

    WarpQuake/WarpQuake
    WarpQuake/id1/pak0.pak
    WarpQuake/id1/pak1.pak      (registered version)

Start it from its icon or from a Shell. On the first start an ASL requester
asks for the screen mode; the choice is saved (WarpQuake.mode) and can be
changed in the game, or asked again with -asl.

Options (Shell)
---------------

    -asl                    choose the screen mode again
    -bpp 8 | -bpp 16        only modes of that depth
    -width W -height H      the mode nearest W x H
    -modeid 0x...           this mode
    -mem <MB>               game memory, 16 by default
    -nosound                no sound
    -ahireq                 choose the AHI mode with AHI's requester
    -ahimode 0x... -ahifreq <Hz>   AHI mode and rate for this run
    +<command>              any console command, e.g. +timedemo demo1

Console variables (saved in config.cfg)
---------------------------------------

    vid_blit 0|1|2          how frames reach the screen: 0 = OS call,
                            1 = lock + copy, 2 = lock + MOVE16 (fastest on
                            a Warp board)
    in_rawmouse 1           raw mouse counts (0: Intuition's mouse events)
    m_filter 0              1 averages each frame's mouse movement with
                            the last one's
    v_rgbflash 1            16 bpp: damage and bonus screen flashes (0: off,
                            a little faster)
    v_watercolor ""         the under-water tint as R,G,B[,strength], e.g.
                            130,80,50 for id's brown water

The console is on the key left of 1; Esc opens the menu.

Not yet
-------

No networking, no CD audio or music. screenshot works at 8 bpp only.

